From: hmaarrfk <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>
Subject: npu-nn-cost-model: do not force -Werror on the cost model targets

npu_compiler builds npu-nn-cost-model as a vendored third-party dependency and
its thirdparty/CMakeLists.txt strips -Werror from the global flags for that
reason, but vpunn_common_settings adds -Werror back as a target compile
option. With GCC 15, libstdc++'s new_allocator.h trips a
-Wfree-nonheap-object false positive in workload_cost_evaluator.cpp and
vpu_layer_cost_model.cpp, which then fails the build. Keep the warnings, drop
-Werror.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 1f22fbc..077f714 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ if(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang|GNU")
     message(STATUS "Setting GCC/Clang specific flags for common settings")
 
     target_compile_options(vpunn_common_settings PUBLIC
-            -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic -Wdouble-promotion -Wfloat-conversion
+            -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wdouble-promotion -Wfloat-conversion
             $<$<CONFIG:Debug>:-g>
             $<$<CONFIG:Release>:-O3>
         )
